     "id": "f9a9a63",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "text-editor",
     "settings": {
      "editor": "<p>Schnitz meals are hearty. A classic <strong>Schnitzel &amp; Chips</strong> comes in at roughly <strong>779 calories (3,259 kJ)</strong>, a <strong>Parma &amp; Chips</strong> at about <strong>897 calories</strong>, and a <strong>Loaded Schnitzel &amp; Chips</strong> can reach around <strong>1,150 calories</strong>. For comparison, the average Australian adult daily intake used on food labels is 8,700 kJ (about 2,080 calories).</p><p>The figures on this page come from third-party nutrition databases and public sources. They are estimates &#8211; serving sizes, crumbs and sauces change the numbers. Where we do not have a reliable figure we leave it blank instead of guessing.</p>"
     },
     "elements": []
